\title{01 · Kernel (stage 0)}
\taxon{Chapter}
\meta{origin}{design/01-kernel.md}
\meta{layer}{human}
\tag{chapter}

\p{The kernel builds the combinatorial raw material — shape categories, presheaves, simplicial sets, Kan machinery — on top of Mathlib. It is scaffolding: defeq is allowed, Mathlib's \code{CategoryTheory} is used freely, and nothing here is visible past the seal. The kernel is judged only by whether \code{Root/} can be built on it and whether the acceptance tests below are proved.}
